{
  "summary": "Retains files scheduled for pruning in a persistent BlockManager set rather than a local variable in FlushStateToDisk. When a flush fails before updating the block index database, queued files remain pending and are unlinked after the next successful block index write. If a file pending deletion is reallocated for new block writes in FindNextBlockPos, it is removed from the unlink queue.",
  "problem": "When a flush that prunes block files fails prior to writing the block index (for instance due to a block file flush error or failed disk space check), the list of files to prune is lost from the local variable. Subsequent successful flushes commit the pruned state to the index but never delete the physical blk and rev files from disk, leaking disk space until ScanAndUnlinkAlreadyPrunedFiles runs on node restart.",
  "evidence": [
    "Identified in reviewer ryanofsky's post-merge review of #35714 (#7): block file flush errors and CheckDiskSpace() failures return before the block index write, leaving files unlinked until restart.",
    "Author description notes this unblocks unit testing for the kernel pruning refactor (#35627)."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
