  "card": "Validation tracks block and undo files queued for pruning inside BlockManager so they can be deleted across flush retries. Previously, files to prune were held in a local variable in FlushStateToDisk, causing an interrupted flush to mark them pruned in the block index on retry without unlinking the physical files on disk until the next node restart. This resolves an edge case highlighted during review of PR 35714 and unblocks follow-up kernel pruning work in PR 36738 and PR 36739.",
